Tibetan Buddhism is based on the teachings of Buddha, but it has been expanded through the Mahayana path and numerous styles of Hindu yoga.
In essence, Tibetan Buddhism is very profound. It consists of Kundalini yoga, meditation, and the path of all-encompassing love.
Kundalini energy (the power of knowledge) is awakened with the help of Kundalini yoga postures, breathing exercises, mantras, and visualizations.
Tibetan meditation is considered a form of divine yoga. Through visualizing various deities, energy channels are purified, chakras are activated, and a state of enlightened consciousness is created.
Germany was the common enemy that led to cooperation between the USSR and the US during World War II. With the end of the war, the system, the process of development, and cultural clashes began to drive the countries into conflict with one another.
