Traffic flow refers to the study of individual drivers and vehicles traveling between two points and their mutual interactions with each other.
Unfortunately, predicting the flow of traffic is difficult, because drivers' behaviors cannot be predicted with 100% accuracy.
Indeed, drivers tend to maintain a reasonably consistent speed; therefore, traffic flows are somewhat consistent and can be approximately described mathematically.
To better express the traffic flow, the following relationships were established among the three basic characteristics: (1) flow, (2) density, and (3) speed.
